its derivative and applying the initial condition."},"Unit":{"Ar":"بلا وحدة قياس","En":"Dimensionless"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"بالتكامل نحصل على $y=5x^2+C$.","En":"Integration gives $y=5x^2+C$."},{"Ar":"باستخدام $y(0)=6$ يكون الحل $y=5x^2+6$؛ ثم نعوض المدخل المطلوب.","En":"Using $y(0)=6$, the solution is $y=5x^2+6$; then evaluate the requested input."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$131$","En":"$131$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"لا تهمل الشرط الابتدائي.","En":"Do not omit the initial condition."},"FormulaLatex":"y(x)=y(0)+\\int_0^x g(t)\\,dt","Substitution":{"Ar":"$y(5)=5(5)^2+6=131$","En":"$y(5)=5(5)^2+6=131$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$(5x^2+6)'=10x,\\quad y(0)=6$","En":"$(5x^2+6)'=10x,\\quad y(0)=6$"}},"Distractors":[{"ErrorType":"misconception","Reason":{"Ar":"الجزء المتغير يساوي $125$؛ اختيار $132$ يتطلب ثابت تكامل $7$ بدلاً من $6$، فلا يحقق الشرط الابتدائي.","En":"The variable part is $125$; choice $132$ requires integration constant $7$ instead of $6$, violating the initial condition."},"Order":1},{"ErrorType":"misconception","Reason":{"Ar":"الجزء المتغير يساوي $125$؛ اختيار $134$ يتطلب ثابت تكامل $9$ بدلاً من $6$، فلا يحقق الشرط الابتدائي.","En":"The variable part is $125$; choice $134$ requires integration constant $9$ instead of $6$, violating the initial condition."},"Order":2},{"ErrorType":"misconception","Reason":{"Ar":"الجزء المتغير يساوي $125$؛ اختيار $129$ يتطلب ثابت تكامل $4$ بدلاً من $6$، فلا يحقق الشرط الابتدائي.","En":"The variable part is $125$; choice $129$ requires integration constant $4$ instead of $6$, violating the initial condition."},"Order":3},{"ErrorType":"","Reason":null,"Order":4}]}$mw$,$mw$نستعيد الدالة بتكامل مشتقتها واستعمال الشرط الابتدائي.

$y(x)=y(0)+\int_0^x g(t)\,dt$

1. بالتكامل نحصل على $y=5x^2+C$.

2. باستخدام $y(0)=6$ يكون الحل $y=5x^2+6$؛ ثم نعوض المدخل المطلوب.

$y(5)=5(5)^2+6=131$

$131$ بلا وحدة قياس

$(5x^2+6)'=10x,\quad y(0)=6$

لا تهمل الشرط الابتدائي.$mw$,$mw$Recover the function by integrating its derivative and applying the initial condition.

$y(x)=y(0)+\int_0^x g(t)\,dt$

1. Integration gives $y=5x^2+C$.

2. Using $y(0)=6$, the solution is $y=5x^2+6$; then evaluate the requested input.

$y(5)=5(5)^2+6=131$

$131$ Dimensionless

$(5x^2+6)'=10x,\quad y(0)=6$

Do not omit the initial condition.$mw$),
(580,374,$mw$C750A8FD1C966FF1F74448FAD97B01AECA4E4DA0321F38734F87764AF3629882$mw$,$mw$c32d775b5f7ee3061885fa76eb34938c$mw$,$mw$$mw$,$mw${"Id":374,"StageId":4,"CategoryId":36,"Points":15,"TitleAr":"أوجد نهاية \\(a_n=\\frac{5}{n+1}\\) عندما \\(n\\to\\infty\\).","TitleEn":"Find limit of \\(a_n=\\frac{5}{n+1}\\) as n tends to infinity.","QuestionTextAr":"أوجد نهاية \\(a_n=\\frac{5}{n+1}\\) عندما \\(n\\to\\infty\\).","QuestionTextEn":"Find limit of \\(a_n=\\frac{5}{n+1}\\) as n tends to infinity.","DetailedSolutionAr":"القانون المستخدم: الكسر ذو البسط الثابت والمقام الذي يزداد إلى ما لا نهاية يتقارب إلى الصفر. للمتتالية aₙ = 5/(n+1)، لأي ε > 0 نختار n أكبر من 5/ε، عندها 0 < 5/(n+1) < ε. إذن lim(aₙ) عندما n → ∞ يساوي 0.","DetailedSolutionEn":"Rule used: A constant divided by a denominator increasing without bound has limit zero. For aₙ = 5/(n+1), given any ε > 0 choose n > 5/ε. Then 0 < 5/(n+1) < ε, proving lim(n→∞) aₙ = 0.","YoutubeSolutionUrl":null,"EditorialDetailsJson":null,"Options":[{"Id":1485,"Order":1,"LatexCode":"0","IsCorrect":true},{"Id":1486,"Order":2,"LatexCode":"1","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":1487,"Order":3,"LatexCode":"5","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":1488,"Order":4,"LatexCode":"+\\infty","IsCorrect":false}]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"Hints":[{"Ar":"راقب سلوك الحد مع ازدياد الرتبة.","En":"Examine term behavior as the index increases."},{"Ar":"قارن الكسر بكمية تؤول للصفر.","En":"Compare with a quantity tending to zero."}],"Title":{"Ar":"أوجد نهاية \\(a_n=\\frac{5}{n+1}\\) عندما \\(n\\to\\infty\\).","En":"Find limit of \\(a_n=\\frac{5}{n+1}\\) as n tends to infinity."},"Points":15,"Options":[{"Reason":null,"ErrorType":"","IsCorrect":true,"LatexCode":"0"},{"Reason":{"Ar":"القيمة $1$ موجبة ثابتة، بينما يمكن جعل الحد أصغر من أي مقدار موجب بزيادة $n$.","En":"Choice $1$ is a fixed positive value, whereas increasing $n$ makes the term smaller than any positive amount."},"ErrorType":"misconception","IsCorrect":false,"LatexCode":"1"},{"Reason":{"Ar":"القيمة $5$ موجبة ثابتة، بينما يمكن جعل الحد أصغر من أي مقدار موجب بزيادة $n$.","En":"Choice $5$ is a fixed positive value, whereas increasing $n$ makes the term smaller than any positive amount."},"ErrorType":"misconception","IsCorrect":false,"LatexCode":"5"},{"Reason":{"Ar":"خلط نمو المقام أو الأس مع نمو الحد نفسه؛ الحد يتناقص.","En":"Confuses growth of the denominator or exponent with growth of the term; the term decreases."},"ErrorType":"misconception","IsCorrect":false,"LatexCode":"+\\infty"}],"StageId":4,"Question":{"Ar":"أوجد نهاية \\(a_n=\\frac{5}{n+1}\\) عندما \\(n\\to\\infty\\).","En":"Find limit of \\(a_n=\\frac{5}{n+1}\\) as n tends to infinity."},"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"البسط ثابت والمقام يزداد بلا حد.","En":"A fixed numerator is divided by an unbounded denominator."},"Unit":{"Ar":"بلا وحدة قياس","En":"Dimensionless"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"البسط $5$ ثابت، والمقام يزداد بلا حد.","En":"The numerator $5$ is fixed and the denominator grows without bound."},{"Ar":"لـ $n\\ge1$، لدينا $0<\\frac{5}{n+1}\\le\\frac{5}n$؛ نطبق مبرهنة الحصر.","En":"For $n\\ge1$, $0<\\frac{5}{n+1}\\le\\frac{5}n$; apply the squeeze theorem."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$0$","En":"$0$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"لا تخلط الحد الأول بالنهاية.","En":"Do not confuse the first term with the limit."},"FormulaLatex":"\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\frac{c}{n+1}=0\\quad(c>0)","Substitution":{"Ar":"$\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\frac{5}{n+1}=0$","En":"$\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\frac{5}{n+1}=0$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"لكل $\\varepsilon>0$، يكفي $n>5/\\varepsilon$.","En":"For every $\\varepsilon>0$, $n>5/\\varepsilon$ suffices."}},"TrackIds":[13,20],"CategoryId":36,"PrimarySkillId":72,"DifficultyLevel":1,"SecondarySkillIds":[]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"DifficultyLevel":1,"Hints":[{"Ar":"راقب سلوك الحد مع ازدياد الرتبة.","En":"Examine term behavior as the index increases."},{"Ar":"قارن الكسر بكمية تؤول للصفر.","En":"Compare with a quantity tending to zero."}],"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"البسط ثابت والمقام يزداد بلا حد.","En":"A fixed numerator is divided by an unbounded denominator."},"Unit":{"Ar":"بلا وحدة قياس","En":"Dimensionless"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"البسط $5$ ثابت، والمقام يزداد بلا حد.","En":"The numerator $5$ is fixed and the denominator grows without bound."},{"Ar":"لـ $n\\ge1$، لدينا $0<\\frac{5}{n+1}\\le\\frac{5}n$؛ نطبق مبرهنة الحصر.","En":"For $n\\ge1$, $0<\\frac{5}{n+1}\\le\\frac{5}n$; apply the squeeze theorem."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$0$","En":"$0$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"لا تخلط الحد الأول بالنهاية.","En":"Do not confuse the first term with the limit."},"FormulaLatex":"\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\frac{c}{n+1}=0\\quad(c>0)","Substitution":{"Ar":"$\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\frac{5}{n+1}=0$","En":"$\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\frac{5}{n+1}=0$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"لكل $\\varepsilon>0$، يكفي $n>5/\\varepsilon$.","En":"For every $\\varepsilon>0$, $n>5/\\varepsilon$ suffices."}},"Distractors":[{"ErrorType":"","Reason":null,"Order":1},{"ErrorType":"misconception","Reason":{"Ar":"القيمة $1$ موجبة ثابتة، بينما يمكن جعل الحد أصغر من أي مقدار موجب بزيادة $n$.","En":"Choice $1$ is a fixed positive value, whereas increasing $n$ makes the term smaller than any positive amount."},"Order":2},{"ErrorType":"misconception","Reason":{"Ar":"القيمة $5$ موجبة ثابتة، بينما يمكن جعل الحد أصغر من أي مقدار موجب بزيادة $n$.","En":"Choice $5$ is a fixed positive value, whereas increasing $n$ makes the term smaller than any positive amount."},"Order":3},{"ErrorType":"misconception","Reason":{"Ar":"خلط نمو المقام أو الأس مع نمو الحد نفسه؛ الحد يتناقص.","En":"Confuses growth of the denominator or exponent with growth of the term; the term decreases."},"Order":4}]}$mw$,$mw$البسط ثابت والمقام يزداد بلا حد.

$\lim_{n\to\infty}\frac{c}{n+1}=0\quad(c>0)$

1. البسط $5$ ثابت، والمقام يزداد بلا حد.

2. لـ $n\ge1$، لدينا $0<\frac{5}{n+1}\le\frac{5}n$؛ نطبق مبرهنة الحصر.

$\lim_{n\to\infty}\frac{5}{n+1}=0$

$0$ بلا وحدة قياس

لكل $\varepsilon>0$، يكفي $n>5/\varepsilon$.

لا تخلط الحد الأول بالنهاية.$mw$,$mw$A fixed numerator is divided by an unbounded denominator.

$\lim_{n\to\infty}\frac{c}{n+1}=0\quad(c>0)$

1. The numerator $5$ is fixed and the denominator grows without bound.

2. For $n\ge1$, $0<\frac{5}{n+1}\le\frac{5}n$; apply the squeeze theorem.

$\lim_{n\to\infty}\frac{5}{n+1}=0$

$0$ Dimensionless

For every $\varepsilon>0$, $n>5/\varepsilon$ suffices.

Do not confuse the first term with the limit.$mw$),
(581,375,$mw$F1173D3EBB27ADDF5AEBDCAA197F7331A2EF4F92F7C43EFB06B5C51813D078BA$mw$,$mw$474e275b6afd0a5f6e99b68476955c07$mw$,$mw$$mw$,$mw${"Id":375,"StageId":4,"CategoryId":36,"Points":15,"TitleAr":"ما نهاية \\(a_n=(\\frac{1}{5})^n\\) عندما \\(n\\to\\infty\\)؟","TitleEn":"Find the limit of \\(a_n=(\\frac{1}{5})^n\\) as n tends to infinity.","QuestionTextAr":"ما نهاية \\(a_n=(\\frac{1}{5})^n\\) عندما \\(n\\to\\infty\\)؟","QuestionTextEn":"Find the limit of \\(a_n=(\\frac{1}{5})^n\\) as n tends to infinity.","DetailedSolutionAr":"القانون المستخدم: إذا كان |r| < 1 فإن المتتالية الهندسية rⁿ تتقارب إلى الصفر. في حالتنا r = 1/5، وهو بين الصفر والواحد؛ بالتالي aₙ = (1/5)ⁿ = 1/5ⁿ. ومع زيادة n يكبر المقام 5ⁿ بلا حد، لذا lim(aₙ) = 0.","DetailedSolutionEn":"Rule used: For a geometric sequence rⁿ with |r| < 1, the terms tend to zero. Here r = 1/5 lies strictly between 0 and 1, so aₙ = (1/5)ⁿ = 1/5ⁿ. As n increases, 5ⁿ grows without bound; hence lim aₙ = 0.","YoutubeSolutionUrl":null,"EditorialDetailsJson":null,"Options":[{"Id":1489,"Order":1,"LatexCode":"1","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":1490,"Order":2,"LatexCode":"\\frac{1}{5}","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":1491,"Order":3,"LatexCode":"+\\infty","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":1492,"Order":4,"LatexCode":"0","IsCorrect":true}]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"Hints":[{"Ar":"راقب سلوك الحد مع ازدياد الرتبة.","En":"Examine term behavior as the index increases."},{"Ar":"تحقق من القيمة المطلقة للأساس.","En":"Check the absolute value of the base."}],"Title":{"Ar":"ما نهاية \\(a_n=(\\frac{1}{5})^n\\) عندما \\(n\\to\\infty\\)؟","En":"Find the limit of \\(a_n=(\\frac{1}{5})^n\\) as n tends to infinity."},"Points":15,"Options":[{"Reason":{"Ar":"القيمة $1$ موجبة ثابتة، بينما يمكن جعل الحد أصغر من أي مقدار موجب بزيادة $n$.","En":"Choice $1$ is a fixed positive value, whereas increasing $n$ makes the term smaller than any positive amount."},"ErrorType":"misconception","IsCorrect":false,"LatexCode":"1"},{"Reason":{"Ar":"القيمة $\\frac{1}{5}$ موجبة ثابتة، بينما يمكن جعل الحد أ